  "summary": "I worked all 14 results-inbox items: 9 were there when I started and 5 arrived while I worked. 12 are closed. 2 are deliberately not closed: one waits on a final report and one went to RN triage because the patient's identity didn't match.\n\n**Original items**\n- **pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram:** no cause found for the blood in his urine. It showed an incidental 4 mm left lower lobe lung nodule. I first ordered a 12-month chest CT (sr-t0001) with a tracking task (task-t0002), messaged him and wrote a note. A later arrival changed this (see below).\n- **pt-0016, TSH:** normal; closed.\n- **pt-0016, potassium:** the lab corrected the critical 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal. I acted on the corrected value and closed it.\n- **pt-0007, preliminary CT angiogram of the chest:** the final report (dr-00084) shows no clot in the lungs. The \"nodule\" on the first read was a blood vessel, and no follow-up is needed. Closed.\n- **pt-0007, BMP:** creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 hours, which meets the acute kidney injury (AKI) rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, put his naproxen on hold, messaged him today and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0065 Lakeshore fax (lung screening addendum, Lung-RADS 4A):** the date of birth and MRN on the fax don't match our patient, and it doesn't fit her screening history. I placed no orders and sent no notice. I handed the item to RN triage to call Lakeshore, get the finding to the right patient's clinician and correct the record. It stays open with them.\n- **pt-0064, ED BMP from 9/26:** creatinine 1.36, with no earlier value in the 48-hour or 7-day window, so it doesn't meet the AKI rule. Closed with no action.\n- **pt-0033, BMP:** creatinine 1.31. I left out the 10/21 value because it was entered in error. Compared with 1.27 on 10/17 it doesn't meet the AKI rule. Closed with no action.\n- **pt-0008, potassium 6.4:** it was flagged as hemolyzed, so I first ordered an urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0017) and messaged him. A correction later changed this (see below).\n\n**Items that arrived while I worked**\n- **pt-0008 correction:** the specimen was not hemolyzed after all, so the 6.4 stands and the stricter critical-potassium rule applies. I ordered a stat BMP for today and sent a stat message to on-call. I also sent him a correction asking him to come in today. His medication list has nothing that raises potassium and can safely be held, so I changed none. A note explains the change. The stat draw replaces the urgent repeat.\n- **pt-0006 Lakeshore addendum:** he is already in lung cancer screening, and the left lower lobe nodule is the one being followed there. The screening CT is now Lung-RADS 3 (probably benign) with a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, and they recommend a repeat in 6 months. Under policy that means the next screening CT, not my 12-month CT. I ordered the screening CT for a window ending 11/14, created a tracking task, sent him a corrected message and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0033, creatinine 1.78 (evening of 10/22):** up from 1.31 that morning, which meets the AKI rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, notified her today and wrote a note. The note flags her hydrochlorothiazide, started 10/17, for you to review.\n- **pt-0064, creatinine 1.48 (10/22):** up from 0.88 on 10/21, which meets the AKI rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, held her naproxen, notified her today and wrote a note.\n- **pt-0007, preliminary chest X-ray:** no final report has been issued yet, so per policy I left it open.\n\n**Needs your follow-up**\n- **Orders I couldn't cancel:** the tools can't cancel lab or imaging orders, or a tracking task that isn't an inbox item.\n  - The replaced 12-month CT for pt-0006 (sr-t0001) and its tracking task are still active. I asked Scheduling (task-t0028) not to book it and to remove both.\n  - The urgent BMP for pt-0008 (sr-t0017) is still active too. It is marked as replaced in his chart, but I didn't send a separate cancellation request.\n- **Medication holds beyond policy:** the naproxen holds for pt-0007 and pt-0064 were my own decision; the policy only requires the repeat BMP and patient notice. Please confirm or reverse them.\n\nI didn't work your messages queue, which has 7 open refill requests.",
